&Q000760 = The debate between Hoe and Plough
@composite
#project: etcslatf/inter
#atf: use unicode
#atf: use math
#etcsl: text-id=c.5.3.1
#key: after http://etcsl.orinst.ox.ac.uk/cgi-bin/etcsl.cgi?text=c.5.3.1&display=Crit&charenc=gcirc#

1. e {ŋiš}al-e {ŋiš}al-e {ŋiš}al-e sa la₂-e
#tr.en: O the Hoe, the Hoe, the Hoe, tied together with thongs;
#lem: e[vocative interjection]; al[hoe]; al[hoe]; al[hoe]; sa[sinew]; la[hang]
#etcsl: line-id=1

#etcsl#cite Cited in OB catalogue from Nibru, at Philadelphia, 0.2.01, line 25; OB catalogue in the Louvre, 0.2.02, line 16; OB catalogue from Urim (U2), 0.2.04, line 18

2. {ŋiš}al-e {ŋiš}asal₂-e zu₂ {ŋiš}ma-nu-e
#tr.en: the Hoe, made from poplar, with a tooth of ash;
#lem: al[hoe]; asal[poplar]; zu[tooth]; manu[wood]
#etcsl: line-id=2

3. {ŋiš}al-e {ŋiš}šinig-e zu₂ ŋiš-ab-ba-ke₄
#tr.en: the Hoe, made from tamarisk, with a tooth of sea-thorn;
#lem: al[hoe]; šinig[tamarisk]; zu[tooth]; ŋešabak[tree]
#etcsl: line-id=3

4. {ŋiš}al-e zu₂ 2-e zu₂ 4-e
#tr.en: the Hoe, double-toothed, four-toothed; the Hoe,
#lem: al[hoe]; zu[tooth]; n; zu[tooth]; n
#etcsl: line-id=4

5. {ŋiš}al-e dumu ukur₃-ra šag₄ {tug₂}niŋ₂-dara₂ kar-re
#tr.en: child of the poor,
#lem: al[hoe]; dumu[child]; ukur[poor]; šag[heart]; niŋdara[rag]; kar[flee]
#etcsl: line-id=5

6. {ŋiš}al-e {ŋiš}apin-na du₁₄ ga-na nam-mi-ŋar
#tr.en: …… bereft even of a loin-cloth (?) -- the Hoe started a quarrel …… with the Plough.
#lem: al[hoe]; apin[(seed) plow]; dud[combat]; gana[come on!]; ŋar[put]
#etcsl: line-id=6

7. {ŋiš}al-e {ŋiš}apin-na a-da-min₃ dug₄-ga
#tr.en: The Hoe having engaged in a dispute with the Plough,
#lem: al[hoe]; apin[(seed) plow]; adamin[contest]; dug[speak]
#etcsl: line-id=7

8. {ŋiš}al-e {ŋiš}apin-na gu₃ am₃-ma-de₂-e
#tr.en: the Hoe addressed the Plough: @q[Hoe,Plough]{“Plough,
#lem: al[hoe]; apin[(seed) plow]; gu[voice]; de[pour]
#etcsl: line-id=8

9. {ŋiš}apin i₃-gid₂-de₃-en gid₂-da-zu nam-ŋu₁₀
#tr.en: you draw furrows -- what does your furrowing matter to me?
#lem: apin[(seed) plow]; gid[long]; gid[long]; anam[what]
#etcsl: line-id=9

10. i₃-lagab-be₂-en lagab-ba-zu nam-ŋu₁₀
#tr.en: You break clods -- what does your clod-breaking matter to me?
#lem: lagab[break into clods]; lagab[break into clods]; anam[what]
#etcsl: line-id=10

11. a u₃-ba-ni-ib-e₃ nu-mu-e-da-an-uš₂-en
#tr.en: When water overflows you cannot dam it up.
#lem: a[water]; e[leave]; uš[shut off]
#etcsl: line-id=11

12. sahar {ŋiš}dusu-e nu-mu-e-da-an-si-si
#tr.en: You cannot fill baskets with earth. You cannot press (?) clay to make bricks.
#lem: sahar[soil]; dupsik[basket (for carrying earth and bricks)]; si[fill]
#etcsl: line-id=12

13. im nu-barag-e-en šeg₁₂ nu-du₃-e-en
#tr.en: You cannot lay foundations or build a house.
#lem: im[clay]; barag[press?]; šeg[brick]; du[build]
#etcsl: line-id=13

14. uš ki nu-ŋa₂-ŋa₂-an e₂ nu-du₃-du₃-en
#tr.en: You cannot strengthen an old wall's base.
#lem: uš[foundation]; ki[place]; ŋar[put]; e[house]; du[build]
#etcsl: line-id=14

15. e₂-ŋar₈ sumun-na ur₂-bi nu-us₂-en
#tr.en: You cannot put a roof on a good man's house.
#lem: egar[wall]; sumun[old]; ur[root]; us[accompany]
#etcsl: line-id=15

16. ur₃ lu₂ zid-da-ke₄ e₂ nu-um-ŋa₂-ŋa₂-an
#tr.en: Plough, you cannot straighten the town squares.
#lem: ur[roof]; lu[person]; zid[right]; e[house]; ŋar[put]
#etcsl: line-id=16

17. {ŋiš}apin sila daŋal-la si nu-um-sa₂-sa₂-en
#tr.en: Plough,
#lem: apin[(seed) plow]; sila[street]; daŋal[wide]; si[horn]; sa[equal]
#etcsl: line-id=17

18. {ŋiš}apin i₃-gid₂-de₃-en gid₂-da-zu nam-ŋu₁₀
#tr.en: you draw furrows -- what does your furrowing matter to me?
#lem: apin[(seed) plow]; gid[long]; gid[long]; anam[what]
#etcsl: line-id=18

19. i₃-lagab-be₂-en lagab-ba-zu nam-ŋu₁₀
#tr.en: You make clods -- what does your clod-making matter to me?”}
#lem: lagab[break into clods]; lagab[break into clods]; anam[what]
#etcsl: line-id=19

20. {ŋiš}apin-e {ŋiš}al-e gu₃ am₃-ma-de₂-e
#tr.en: The Plough addressed the Hoe: @q[Plough,Hoe]{“I am the Plough,
#lem: apin[(seed) plow]; al[hoe]; gu[voice]; de[pour]
#etcsl: line-id=20

